  "label": "User projected onto the visual material of the seated monarchs",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of Queen Elizabeth II and Prince Charles, who are depicted as symbols of the British government and monarchy. The meme uses their image to represent the 'Brits' or the entity being referred to in the text, implying that the government (embodied by the monarchy) is responsible for the policy of gun control and the subsequent enforcement of TV licensing laws. This projection is implicit, as the user is expected to identify with the 'Brits' or the nation as a whole, represented by these national symbols.",
